First surviving convergent: j=23, K/k = 217976794617/137528045312 (m_max = 5.10126e+22).
Legendre threshold: k <= sqrt(3 M0 ln 2 / 2) = 4.9547667e+10; every cycle with k below it has K/k a convergent, hence k >= q_23 = 137528045312 > threshold: contradiction.
So (Legendre route) every nontrivial Syracuse cycle has more than 4.9547667e+10 odd steps. NOTE (audit E): the plain ledger over convergents omits intermediate fractions; at 2^71 the semiconvergent (p_21+p_22)/(q_21+q_22) = 114208327604/72057431991 has budget 3780.4*2^60 > 2^71 and is the only admissible fraction with k < q_23 (Stern-Brocot enumeration, audit_E_farey.py), so Eliahou's full method gives k >= 72,057,431,991; Hercher Cor. 29 (Theorem 27 factor 3/4 + computation, conditional on X_0 >= 3*2^69, met by Barina 2025) gives k > 1.375e11, and then the next admissible denominator is q_23 = 137528045312.
  if |theta - p/q| > q^(-2) for all q, a cycle with minimum >= M0 needs k > (3 M0 ln 2)^(1/2) = 7.0071e+10
  if |theta - p/q| > q^(-3) for all q, a cycle with minimum >= M0 needs k > (3 M0 ln 2)^(1/3) = 1.69965e+7
  if |theta - p/q| > q^(-5) for all q, a cycle with minimum >= M0 needs k > (3 M0 ln 2)^(1/5) = 21787.9
  if |theta - p/q| > q^(-8.616) for all q, a cycle with minimum >= M0 needs k > (3 M0 ln 2)^(1/8.616) = 329.257
  if |theta - p/q| > q^(-14.3) for all q, a cycle with minimum >= M0 needs k > (3 M0 ln 2)^(1/14.3) = 32.8744
  the actual continued fraction (first 40 partial quotients <= 55) behaves like mu = 2 in this range: m_max(j) ~ a_(j+1) q_j^2 / (3 ln 2)
